WEBVTT

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:07.472
First Officer's Personal Log,
Stardate 49005.3.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.771
The Captain has granted me
the use of a shuttlecraft

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.642
so that I may perform
the pakra... a solitary ritual

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.807
commemorating the anniversary
of my father's death.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.311
A- koo-chee-moya.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.010
I pray on this day of memories

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.416
to speak to my father...

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:58.948
the one whom the wind
called... Kolopak.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:02.621
Though I am far from his bones,

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.256
perhaps there is a spirit
in these unnamed skies

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:09.462
who will find him
and honor him with my song.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.106
A- koo-chee-moya.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.642
There. You see?

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.876
We should teach them the price

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.116
of displaying their markings
in our space.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.885
I'll go.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.085
Let Kar do it this time.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.559
He's not ready.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.561
He thinks he is.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.994
He's been demanding
a chance for weeks

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.395
to earn his name.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.456
Do you really believe
he could do this?

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.968
Can you honestly say
you knew you were ready

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.095
for your first mission, Haliz?

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.936
Tell him.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:51.535
Tell him today is the day
he will finally be called Ogla.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.821
Computer, report.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:11.092
The shuttlecraft
has sustained phaser fire.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.962
Minor damage to aft shields.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.260
Source?

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.794
A Kazon spacecraft,
closing at 195, mark 6.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.677
Computer, open a channel
to the Kazon vessel.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.982
This is Commander Chakotay

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.987
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.920
Why have you fired on me?

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.619
You are in Kazon-Ogla space,
Federation.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.423
I wasn't aware of that.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.827
I have no hostile intentions.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.626
Power down your weapons
and I'll leave.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.361
No one who violates
Ogla space leaves.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:52.337
Look, son, my starship is
only a few light-years away.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.135
I am not your son, Federation.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.539
I am your executioner.

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:47.949
Chakotay to Kazon vessel.

00:04:47.986 --> 00:04:49.578
Listen carefully.

00:04:49.621 --> 00:04:51.646
I do not want a fight.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.420
Stand down, or I'll be forced
to return fire.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:21.077
Chakotay to Kazon vessel.

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:22.086
I have established

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.951
a direct weapons lock
on your engine core.

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:25.455
This is my final warning.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.586
If you don't stand down,
I will destroy your ship.

00:05:34.799 --> 00:05:35.766
All right.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.961
If that's the way
you want to play it.

00:05:46.878 --> 00:05:49.938
Chakotay to Kazon vessel.
Do you read me?

00:05:49.981 --> 00:05:52.279
Computer,
are there any life signs

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:53.511
inside the Kazon vessel?

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.850
Affirmative. One life sign.

00:05:55.887 --> 00:05:58.651
Kazon ship,
your engine core is critical.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.885
You have less
than 30 seconds to evacuate.

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:01.858
Do you read me?

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.522
If you have an escape pod,
you must eject now.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.024
Computer,

00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:12.696
establish a transporter lock
on the life-form.

00:06:12.737 --> 00:06:15.035
Acknowledged.
Targeting scanners.

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:17.166
Prepare to beam him aboard.

00:06:17.208 --> 00:06:18.641
Scanners locked.

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:19.666
Energize.

00:06:32.991 --> 00:06:34.618
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:06:37.662 --> 00:06:40.256
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:06:40.298 --> 00:06:43.165
Computer, damage report.

00:06:43.201 --> 00:06:46.193
Long-range communications,
lateral sensor array

00:06:46.237 --> 00:06:48.569
and aft shields are off-line.

00:06:48.607 --> 00:06:50.097
Great!

00:06:51.676 --> 00:06:53.871
Welcome aboard.

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:08.253
It's not that I feel

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:10.124
that I'm not
making contributions

00:07:10.161 --> 00:07:12.629
as chef and morale officer.

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:15.394
You're making significant
contributions, Neelix.

00:07:15.433 --> 00:07:17.594
Well, if you insist, but...

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:19.103
I can't imagine
how Lieutenant Ayala

00:07:19.137 --> 00:07:22.538
would be handling the separation
from his children without you.

00:07:22.574 --> 00:07:25.338
He misses his boys terribly.

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:27.572
I wish I could do more for him.

00:07:27.612 --> 00:07:29.944
And your meals
are getting to be...

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:31.482
Yes?

00:07:31.516 --> 00:07:33.882
Almost certainly...

00:07:33.918 --> 00:07:36.409
a highlight of every day.

00:07:36.454 --> 00:07:38.922
Oh, Captain!

00:07:38.957 --> 00:07:41.425
You always know
how to touch one's heart.

00:07:41.459 --> 00:07:42.858
Thank you.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:45.294
When I signed on,

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:46.888
I promised you that...

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:52.498
I promised you
that I would stand by your side

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:55.233
through every danger
this Quadrant has to offer...

00:07:55.273 --> 00:07:58.765
as guide, as strategist,
as explorer, as adventurer...

00:07:58.810 --> 00:07:59.970
Yes?

00:08:02.447 --> 00:08:04.540
I feel...

00:08:04.582 --> 00:08:07.608
under-utilized.

00:08:07.652 --> 00:08:10.780
I can swashbuckle
with the best of them.

00:08:10.822 --> 00:08:11.914
You weren't invited

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.515
to the holodeck
defense simulations, were you?

00:08:14.559 --> 00:08:15.583
No!

00:08:15.627 --> 00:08:16.924
Captain, you are needed
on the Bridge.

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:17.927
On my way.

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:20.328
I'll see to it
you're invited next time.

00:08:20.365 --> 00:08:23.926
And now, Mr. Neelix, please...
join me on the Bridge.

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:25.367
Yes, sir.

00:08:25.403 --> 00:08:27.132
Ma'am... Captain.

00:08:29.174 --> 00:08:30.266
We are ready to depart.

00:08:30.308 --> 00:08:32.276
However, Commander Chakotay
has still not returned.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.368
Have you tried hailing him?

00:08:33.411 --> 00:08:35.936
On all frequencies.
No response.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.538
When was the last time
we heard from him?

00:08:37.582 --> 00:08:39.049
More than six hours ago.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.490
Well, according to his
flight plan, he's not far.

00:08:47.525 --> 00:08:49.322
We'll just have to go get him.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.328
I want all away teams
back on board now.

00:08:51.362 --> 00:08:52.624
Mr. Paris, plot a course

00:08:52.664 --> 00:08:54.291
for Chakotay's
last known coordinates.

00:08:54.332 --> 00:08:55.321
Aye, Captain.

00:09:09.447 --> 00:09:11.176
What am I doing here?

00:09:13.384 --> 00:09:14.783
You're welcome.

00:09:14.819 --> 00:09:15.911
What?

00:09:15.987 --> 00:09:17.352
It's a human expression.

00:09:17.388 --> 00:09:19.720
You thank me for saving
your life, I say,

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:20.918
"You're welcome."

00:09:26.097 --> 00:09:27.826
I accept your surrender.

00:09:27.866 --> 00:09:29.925
Look!

00:09:30.034 --> 00:09:32.366
I promise you, as soon
as we get back to Voyager,

00:09:32.403 --> 00:09:34.701
we'll find a Kazon ship
and hand you over to them.

00:09:38.476 --> 00:09:40.239
You should have let me die.

00:09:40.278 --> 00:09:42.473
I'm not in the habit
of killing children.

00:09:42.514 --> 00:09:47.110
Warning. Alien vessel
approaching at 022 mark 8.

00:09:50.622 --> 00:09:51.816
What's your name, son?

00:09:51.856 --> 00:09:52.948
What?

00:09:53.024 --> 00:09:54.355
Your name?

00:09:54.392 --> 00:09:56.360
Why do you want to know my name?

00:09:56.394 --> 00:09:58.828
I want to let them know
you're on board.

00:10:03.668 --> 00:10:05.431
I'm called Kar.

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:08.633
Computer, open a channel.

00:10:10.308 --> 00:10:13.334
Kazon vessel, I have

00:10:13.378 --> 00:10:15.869
a young man on board
you might know.

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:17.643
He goes by the name of Kar.

00:10:17.682 --> 00:10:20.344
I'd say he's about 13.

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:22.979
I'd like to arrange
for his transfer

00:10:23.021 --> 00:10:24.386
before I return to my ship.

00:10:26.624 --> 00:10:28.990
Computer, confirm
channel is open.

00:10:29.027 --> 00:10:31.996
Confirmed.
Transmission has been received.

00:10:33.264 --> 00:10:35.232
Talk to them.
Tell them you're okay.

00:10:38.403 --> 00:10:42.396
Warning. Kazon vessel
has engaged a tractor beam.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.340
Full reverse.

00:10:44.375 --> 00:10:46.002
Unable to comply.

00:10:46.044 --> 00:10:49.036
Tractor force exceeds
available engine power.

00:10:50.381 --> 00:10:51.814
They're pulling us in.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.784
Kill me.

00:10:57.422 --> 00:10:58.889
Please!

00:11:03.628 --> 00:11:05.357
Why are you so eager
for me to kill you?

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:10.866
Because there are worse things
than being killed by your enemy.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.146
Look, if you check
your long-range sensors,

00:11:28.186 --> 00:11:29.881
you'll find a big ship
out there.

00:11:29.921 --> 00:11:31.445
It's called Voyager,

00:11:31.489 --> 00:11:33.480
and by now,
it's on its way to find me.

00:11:33.524 --> 00:11:34.513
Kar.

00:11:34.559 --> 00:11:36.891
I told Razik you weren't ready.

00:11:36.928 --> 00:11:39.726
I have a fair idea
of why I'm here,

00:11:39.764 --> 00:11:41.197
but why are they
doing this to you?

00:11:41.232 --> 00:11:42.995
I was ready, Haliz.

00:11:43.101 --> 00:11:45.160
Ready to kill or die.

00:11:45.203 --> 00:11:47.000
I felt the flames touch my skin.

00:11:47.038 --> 00:11:49.836
Go back in, Kar.

00:11:56.681 --> 00:11:58.342
It was this fool...

00:11:58.383 --> 00:12:00.715
this... Federation,

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:03.619
who doesn't even have
the courage to kill his enemies.

00:12:03.655 --> 00:12:04.713
He pulled me out

00:12:04.756 --> 00:12:06.781
with that transporter
we've heard about.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.430
Like the Nistrim
and the Relora before you...

00:12:16.467 --> 00:12:17.661
you come into our space,

00:12:17.702 --> 00:12:19.727
showing off your uniforms

00:12:19.771 --> 00:12:23.104
and displaying the markings
of your... Federation

00:12:23.141 --> 00:12:28.169
with no respect, as if you
own this part of space.

00:12:29.647 --> 00:12:31.478
But it belongs to us!

00:12:36.788 --> 00:12:38.119
I tried to kill him, Haliz!

00:12:43.861 --> 00:12:45.829
I want to see Razik.

00:12:48.266 --> 00:12:50.700
Tell Razik I demand to see him.

00:12:53.304 --> 00:12:55.772
Who's Razik?

00:12:58.309 --> 00:12:59.640
You tell this Razik

00:12:59.677 --> 00:13:02.441
that Federation Commander
Chakotay demands to see him.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.107
What are you doing?

00:13:05.783 --> 00:13:07.944
Razik is obviously your leader.

00:13:08.052 --> 00:13:10.077
I'm hoping if he's strong
enough to be in command,

00:13:10.121 --> 00:13:11.816
he's wise enough
to listen to reason.

00:13:16.894 --> 00:13:18.521
You see this?

00:13:18.563 --> 00:13:20.963
This is debris
from a Nistrim frigate.

00:13:21.065 --> 00:13:23.693
The man you are demanding to see
destroyed it,

00:13:23.735 --> 00:13:26.067
killing more than 100
in a single shot.

00:13:26.104 --> 00:13:28.902
Before that,
his name was only Ra.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:31.500
Now he is called Jal Razik.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:35.604
And this tunic belonged
to a Relora warrior.

00:13:35.646 --> 00:13:38.206
He was killed by the bare hands

00:13:38.249 --> 00:13:41.082
of another Ogla,
called only Hali.

00:13:41.119 --> 00:13:44.179
Now that man is
called Jal Haliz,

00:13:44.222 --> 00:13:45.917
one of our greatest fighters.

00:13:45.957 --> 00:13:47.720
And this bracelet belonged

00:13:47.759 --> 00:13:49.590
to the man
who killed my brother.

00:13:49.627 --> 00:13:53.324
My brother, Jal Kinell...

00:13:53.364 --> 00:13:57.926
who earned his Ogla name
by dying bravely in battle.

00:13:57.969 --> 00:14:02.804
But I... I will never earn
my name in life or in death,

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:05.638
and I have you
to thank for that.

00:14:15.686 --> 00:14:18.621
We're approaching Chakotay's
last known coordinates, Captain.

00:14:18.656 --> 00:14:21.056
All stop.
Full sensor scan, Mr. Kim.

00:14:23.461 --> 00:14:24.758
I'm picking up floating debris

00:14:24.796 --> 00:14:28.425
composed of duranium, magnesite
and electroceramics.

00:14:28.466 --> 00:14:30.661
Also heavy traces
of carbon residue.

00:14:31.669 --> 00:14:32.829
Bridge to Engineering.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.338
Prepare to receive debris
samples for analysis.

00:14:35.373 --> 00:14:36.362
Aye, Captain.

00:14:37.675 --> 00:14:39.267
Transport complete.

00:14:40.511 --> 00:14:41.978
Captain, I am detecting

00:14:42.013 --> 00:14:44.709
an ion trail leading away
from this location.

00:14:44.749 --> 00:14:46.080
Chakotay's shuttle?

00:14:46.117 --> 00:14:47.948
The signature of the radiation
is not consistent

00:14:47.985 --> 00:14:50.249
with Federation
propulsion systems.

00:14:50.288 --> 00:14:52.779
So what are we saying here?

00:14:52.824 --> 00:14:55.486
That someone blew up Chakotay's
shuttle and then took off?

00:14:55.526 --> 00:14:57.619
That's speculation, Mr. Paris,

00:14:57.662 --> 00:14:59.721
but that trail's
the only clue we have

00:14:59.764 --> 00:15:01.493
to Chakotay's whereabouts.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.933
Laying in a course.

00:15:04.001 --> 00:15:05.229
Engage.

00:15:19.951 --> 00:15:21.782
Hello, Kar.

00:15:28.991 --> 00:15:31.391
I never thought I would
see you like this.

00:15:31.427 --> 00:15:32.553
It was not my fault.

00:15:32.595 --> 00:15:33.857
It was his technology.

00:15:35.031 --> 00:15:37.363
Don't make excuses, Kar.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:40.392
An Ogla has no room for excuses.

00:15:41.571 --> 00:15:44.506
No. No excuses.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.667
I forgive you.

00:15:46.709 --> 00:15:48.472
Know that in your heart.

00:15:50.279 --> 00:15:52.247
No, please...

00:16:02.892 --> 00:16:05.656
You will eat
at my right hand tonight.

00:16:09.198 --> 00:16:10.722
Why did you save him?

00:16:10.766 --> 00:16:14.065
It's a very ineffective
way of waging war.

00:16:14.103 --> 00:16:16.037
I'm not at war with you.

00:16:16.072 --> 00:16:18.802
I wish I could say the same.

00:16:18.841 --> 00:16:20.706
We're not familiar
with this part of space.

00:16:20.743 --> 00:16:24.611
If I'd seen a map identifying
this as Kazon-Ogla territory,

00:16:24.647 --> 00:16:26.808
I wouldn't have been
anywhere near it.

00:16:26.849 --> 00:16:31.149
Unfortunately, our territorial
claims change every day.

00:16:31.187 --> 00:16:34.452
Maps do not serve us well.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:37.948
You did him a great disservice,
you know.

00:16:38.027 --> 00:16:39.619
I guess if he had killed me,

00:16:39.662 --> 00:16:42.426
my uniform would have made
you all a fine trophy.

00:16:42.465 --> 00:16:45.559
Your uniform may yet
decorate our wall.

00:16:45.601 --> 00:16:48.661
You may not think
you're at war with us,

00:16:48.704 --> 00:16:50.968
Federation Commander Chakotay,

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:54.134
but everything you are
is a threat to us.

00:16:54.176 --> 00:16:55.803
The Kazon fought long and hard

00:16:55.845 --> 00:16:58.780
for their independence
from uniforms like yours.

00:16:58.814 --> 00:17:02.580
Uniforms, maybe,
but not like mine.

00:17:02.618 --> 00:17:07.885
Your uniforms,
your laws, your technology.

00:17:07.923 --> 00:17:09.720
You are not welcome here.

00:17:14.764 --> 00:17:16.561
Get him something to eat.

00:17:16.599 --> 00:17:18.931
The execution is tonight.

00:17:35.251 --> 00:17:36.650
Well?

00:17:36.686 --> 00:17:38.847
Most of the debris
we've examined

00:17:38.888 --> 00:17:41.083
is composed
of a polyduranide alloy,

00:17:41.123 --> 00:17:42.818
which isn't used
in the construction

00:17:42.858 --> 00:17:44.553
of Federation spacecraft.

00:17:44.593 --> 00:17:47.061
So it wasn't Chakotay's shuttle
that was destroyed.

00:17:47.096 --> 00:17:48.996
This ship was Kazon.

00:17:56.539 --> 00:17:58.769
You get them involved young,
Haliz.

00:17:58.808 --> 00:17:59.968
As soon as they're old enough

00:18:00.009 --> 00:18:02.273
to protect
their younger siblings.

00:18:07.183 --> 00:18:10.778
So they brought you here
to see your first human.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.482
Take a good look...

00:18:13.522 --> 00:18:16.650
you won't see
any hate in my eyes.

00:18:16.692 --> 00:18:18.250
I'm a gentle man

00:18:18.294 --> 00:18:20.489
from a gentle people
who wish you no harm.

00:18:20.529 --> 00:18:21.518
That's enough!

00:18:22.531 --> 00:18:24.522
I know you'd like them
to hate me, Razik,

00:18:24.567 --> 00:18:26.057
but I want their first
impression of humans

00:18:26.102 --> 00:18:27.160
to be a good one.

00:18:27.203 --> 00:18:28.261
You've been brought here

00:18:28.304 --> 00:18:31.273
to learn what it means
to be a Kazon male.

00:18:32.808 --> 00:18:34.605
You all know Kar.

00:18:34.643 --> 00:18:36.508
You've learned to fight
together, haven't you?

00:18:36.545 --> 00:18:41.278
Kar was sent to kill this man
to earn his Ogla name,

00:18:41.317 --> 00:18:43.717
but Kar failed

00:18:43.753 --> 00:18:46.347
and will not earn his name
even in death.

00:18:48.557 --> 00:18:50.047
Who would be willing
to kill the human?

00:18:52.261 --> 00:18:55.492
So much for first impressions,
Federation.

00:18:56.799 --> 00:18:58.892
I'm proud of you.

00:18:58.934 --> 00:19:01.095
Each will get
your chance someday.

00:19:01.137 --> 00:19:04.265
But that's not
what we're here for today.

00:19:05.374 --> 00:19:09.140
We are here to learn
the price of failure in battle.

00:19:12.114 --> 00:19:13.308
Take it.

00:19:13.349 --> 00:19:15.112
What for?

00:19:15.151 --> 00:19:16.482
So that you can kill Kar

00:19:16.519 --> 00:19:18.384
as you should have done
in battle.

00:19:18.421 --> 00:19:22.221
You want me to kill a child
in front of other children.

00:19:22.258 --> 00:19:24.192
What would it accomplish?

00:19:24.226 --> 00:19:27.821
It will teach these little boys
an important lesson.

00:19:27.863 --> 00:19:31.594
And after you do that,
you'll be free to go.

00:19:31.634 --> 00:19:34.102
You may think I want
your friend Kar to die,

00:19:34.136 --> 00:19:36.400
but you'd be wrong.

00:19:36.439 --> 00:19:40.239
I've seen too many Ogla die
at the hands of our enemies.

00:19:40.276 --> 00:19:42.710
That is why you must learn
there are

00:19:42.745 --> 00:19:44.736
no second chances in battle.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.715
That is why Kar must die.

00:19:52.021 --> 00:19:53.283
If I refuse?

00:20:19.148 --> 00:20:21.514
I'll be needing my shuttle back.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.983
Do you really think
you can escape us

00:20:23.085 --> 00:20:24.746
in that little vessel of yours?

00:20:24.787 --> 00:20:26.982
That's a chance
I'm willing to take.

00:20:27.022 --> 00:20:28.614
What about you?

00:20:28.657 --> 00:20:30.454
Let the coward run.

00:20:30.493 --> 00:20:31.983
Prepare his shuttle.

00:20:38.601 --> 00:20:39.693
Want to come?

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.963
There doesn't seem to be
much of a future for you here.

00:20:44.373 --> 00:20:45.567
He'd rather die

00:20:45.608 --> 00:20:48.475
than run like a Calogan dog
with you, Federation.

00:20:55.518 --> 00:20:58.180
If I stay here,
I'll die without a name,

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:01.280
and Razik taught me
only cowards die without a name.

00:21:01.323 --> 00:21:02.415
You won't find your name

00:21:02.458 --> 00:21:04.119
running after the Federation,
Kar.

00:21:04.159 --> 00:21:05.649
Maybe not.

00:21:05.694 --> 00:21:07.662
But that's a chance
I'm willing to take.

00:21:12.501 --> 00:21:14.696
I'll show you how to disable
the weapon systems.

00:21:23.012 --> 00:21:25.276
Will Razik be all right?

00:21:25.314 --> 00:21:26.645
Don't worry.
He's only stunned.

00:21:28.951 --> 00:21:29.975
Didn't take them long

00:21:30.052 --> 00:21:32.213
to get those weapons
back on line, did it?

00:21:32.254 --> 00:21:33.744
Computer, prepare to go to warp.

00:21:33.789 --> 00:21:36.519
No. Their ship is much clumsier
at lower speeds.

00:21:36.559 --> 00:21:38.322
We should try
to outmaneuver them.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.691
You're the boss.

00:21:41.564 --> 00:21:45.000
Initiate evasive pattern
theta two, full impulse.

00:21:45.067 --> 00:21:47.968
I can give you the shield
frequencies of their ship.

00:21:48.003 --> 00:21:49.436
We could hit them back easily.

00:21:49.471 --> 00:21:51.439
It may mean something to you
to die a violent death,

00:21:51.473 --> 00:21:54.340
but I'd like to get out of this
without killing or being killed.

00:21:54.376 --> 00:21:56.936
You'd rather die in your sleep,
a wrinkled old man?

00:21:56.979 --> 00:21:58.241
Sounds about right.

00:22:00.816 --> 00:22:02.340
Computer, damage report.

00:22:02.384 --> 00:22:04.944
Aft shields at 63 percent.

00:22:04.987 --> 00:22:07.455
We're not going
to make it like this.

00:22:07.489 --> 00:22:09.957
Computer, scan
for an M-Class atmosphere.

00:22:10.025 --> 00:22:14.359
There is an M-Class moon
at bearing 108, mark 18.

00:22:14.396 --> 00:22:17.092
Distance 1.9 million kilometers.

00:22:17.132 --> 00:22:18.599
That's Tarok,

00:22:18.634 --> 00:22:21.535
where the Ogla conduct
training exercises.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.628
Anybody training there now?

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:27.702
Computer, lay in a course
to the moon.

00:22:27.743 --> 00:22:29.802
Evasive pattern omega one.

00:22:29.845 --> 00:22:31.039
Maximum impulse.

00:22:39.688 --> 00:22:42.384
Warning. Aft shields
have been penetrated.

00:22:42.424 --> 00:22:43.652
Hull breach is imminent.

00:22:43.692 --> 00:22:45.819
Computer, prepare
for long-range transport.

00:22:45.861 --> 00:22:46.850
Two to beam to the surface.

00:22:46.895 --> 00:22:48.863
Transport is not recommended.

00:22:48.897 --> 00:22:50.831
The moon is out of safety range.

00:23:05.881 --> 00:23:08.281
Captain, the ion trail
is beginning to dissipate.

00:23:08.317 --> 00:23:09.511
All stop.

00:23:09.551 --> 00:23:11.246
I'm picking up debris again.

00:23:11.286 --> 00:23:14.653
More duranium, magnesite,
carbon residue...

00:23:15.824 --> 00:23:17.917
It's the remnants
of another ship.

00:23:19.028 --> 00:23:20.290
Bridge to Engineering.

00:23:20.329 --> 00:23:22.593
Lieutenant Torres, prepare to
receive another debris sample.

00:23:22.631 --> 00:23:23.598
Acknowledged.

00:23:23.632 --> 00:23:25.930
Transport underway.

00:23:29.471 --> 00:23:32.201
Torres to Bridge.
Sample received.

00:23:32.241 --> 00:23:34.903
Let me know when you've
got something, B'Elanna.

00:23:34.943 --> 00:23:37.377
I've got something right now.

00:23:37.413 --> 00:23:40.405
It's a piece
of Chakotay's shuttle.

00:23:54.663 --> 00:23:56.824
Kar...

00:23:56.865 --> 00:23:58.093
It worked?

00:24:01.003 --> 00:24:02.027
The computer said

00:24:02.071 --> 00:24:04.039
that transport
wasn't recommended.

00:24:04.073 --> 00:24:06.405
Didn't say it was impossible.

00:24:08.544 --> 00:24:09.943
With any luck,

00:24:10.045 --> 00:24:13.139
Razik will think we didn't
survive the explosion.

00:24:13.182 --> 00:24:17.175
Then maybe you'll get your name
for dying in battle.

00:24:17.219 --> 00:24:19.483
In battle?!

00:24:19.521 --> 00:24:22.149
That wasn't a battle!

00:24:22.191 --> 00:24:23.954
We didn't even shoot back.

00:24:24.059 --> 00:24:26.527
And now, I'm stranded here.

00:24:26.562 --> 00:24:28.393
With you.

00:24:30.299 --> 00:24:32.631
Yes, you're stranded here
with me.

00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:36.695
And I'm stranded here with you,

00:24:36.739 --> 00:24:38.639
because for some reason
that escapes me at the moment,

00:24:38.674 --> 00:24:40.073
I keep saving your life.

00:24:40.109 --> 00:24:43.237
Now if you want
to hate me for that, fine,

00:24:43.278 --> 00:24:45.872
but I'd really appreciate it
if you kept it to yourself.

00:24:45.914 --> 00:24:47.279
- You...
- To yourself!

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:54.389
First thing we've got to do
is find some shelter

00:24:54.423 --> 00:24:55.981
and get out of this heat.

00:24:56.058 --> 00:24:58.026
Any suggestions?

00:25:05.334 --> 00:25:08.167
I think we're finally beginning
to understand each other.

00:25:12.975 --> 00:25:14.575
You don't know
what you're doing.

00:25:15.943 --> 00:25:18.002
What did I just say?

00:25:20.647 --> 00:25:22.808
Get down.

00:25:25.786 --> 00:25:27.720
What the hell was that?

00:25:27.754 --> 00:25:29.381
A proton beam.

00:25:32.926 --> 00:25:34.257
They're hidden everywhere,

00:25:34.294 --> 00:25:36.728
along with biomagnetic traps
and disrupter snares.

00:25:36.763 --> 00:25:37.752
Charming.

00:25:37.798 --> 00:25:39.060
I told you.

00:25:39.099 --> 00:25:41.158
The Ogla train on this moon.

00:25:41.201 --> 00:25:44.796
I was here myself last year
with Razik.

00:25:44.838 --> 00:25:46.066
So I guess you know
your way around.

00:25:46.106 --> 00:25:48.734
I know that you're
in my territory,

00:25:48.775 --> 00:25:51.300
and if you want to live
to become that wrinkled old man,

00:25:51.345 --> 00:25:53.836
you're going to have to do
what I say.

00:25:55.382 --> 00:25:57.282
Well, it looks like you
just saved my life.

00:25:57.317 --> 00:25:59.683
Twice more and we'll be even.

00:26:01.855 --> 00:26:04.653
I finished analyzing
the shuttle debris

00:26:04.691 --> 00:26:07.159
and I found no evidence
of human remains.

00:26:07.194 --> 00:26:10.027
Then it's possible Chakotay
wasn't killed in the explosion.

00:26:10.063 --> 00:26:11.394
That is correct.

00:26:11.431 --> 00:26:14.093
That's the first good news
I've heard all day.

00:26:14.134 --> 00:26:15.123
Thank you, Doctor.

00:26:15.168 --> 00:26:16.294
My pleasure.

00:26:16.336 --> 00:26:18.930
Now, would you mind having
someone transport this junk

00:26:19.006 --> 00:26:20.473
to the cargo bay?

00:26:22.409 --> 00:26:23.740
It's cluttering up my lab.

00:26:23.777 --> 00:26:25.540
Of course, Doctor.

00:26:25.579 --> 00:26:28.070
All right then,
if Commander Chakotay

00:26:28.115 --> 00:26:30.083
wasn't in the shuttle,
where is he?

00:26:30.117 --> 00:26:32.244
From the dispersal
pattern of the debris,

00:26:32.285 --> 00:26:33.946
we've been able to extrapolate
Chakotay's course

00:26:34.054 --> 00:26:35.681
prior to the explosion.

00:26:35.722 --> 00:26:36.689
It appears he was heading

00:26:36.723 --> 00:26:38.884
for an M-Class moon
in this system.

00:26:38.925 --> 00:26:40.483
And we found a residual
energy displacement

00:26:40.527 --> 00:26:41.789
within the debris field

00:26:41.828 --> 00:26:44.262
that isn't consistent
with the explosion itself.

00:26:44.297 --> 00:26:46.390
You think he may have
transported to that moon.

00:26:46.433 --> 00:26:47.923
We tried to scan the surface,

00:26:47.968 --> 00:26:50.095
but there is intense
radiothermic interference.

00:26:50.137 --> 00:26:51.399
Radiothermic?

00:26:51.438 --> 00:26:52.405
It appears to be coming

00:26:52.439 --> 00:26:54.566
from subterranean
energy sources...

00:26:54.608 --> 00:26:57.634
several carefully concealed
weapon systems... phaser banks,

00:26:57.678 --> 00:26:59.942
force fields,
proton dischargers.

00:26:59.980 --> 00:27:01.277
Kazon.

00:27:01.314 --> 00:27:02.303
When they captured me,

00:27:02.349 --> 00:27:04.214
I saw how they concealed
their weaponry.

00:27:04.251 --> 00:27:07.846
I believe you call them
"booby traps."

00:27:07.888 --> 00:27:11.187
Then this moon is some kind
of Kazon fortification.

00:27:11.224 --> 00:27:13.454
Or it may simply be
a training site.

00:27:13.493 --> 00:27:15.859
For the Kazon, live ammunition

00:27:15.896 --> 00:27:18.490
is a very effective
teaching tool.

00:27:18.532 --> 00:27:21.558
In the absence of evidence
to the contrary

00:27:21.601 --> 00:27:24.365
I choose to believe
Chakotay made it to that moon.

00:27:24.404 --> 00:27:25.928
Mr. Kim, see
if you can determine

00:27:26.039 --> 00:27:28.507
the most probable location
he would've beamed to.

00:27:28.542 --> 00:27:30.772
Lieutenant, you and I
will lead the away team.

00:27:30.811 --> 00:27:33.109
As you wish, Captain,
but I must point out

00:27:33.146 --> 00:27:35.114
that due to radiothermic
interference,

00:27:35.148 --> 00:27:36.809
we will not be able
to communicate with the ship.

00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:38.317
I'm already working
on a dampening field

00:27:38.351 --> 00:27:39.511
to cut through the interference,

00:27:39.553 --> 00:27:42.283
but it'll take several
hours at least.

00:27:42.322 --> 00:27:43.949
I don't want to wait that long,
but keep trying.

00:27:43.990 --> 00:27:46.220
Neelix, Kes, you are
our two Kazon experts.

00:27:46.259 --> 00:27:47.726
Kes, you'll come
with Tuvok and me.

00:27:47.761 --> 00:27:50.059
Neelix, you said
you wanted more to do.

00:27:50.097 --> 00:27:51.587
Well, now's your chance.

00:27:51.631 --> 00:27:53.360
I want you on the Bridge
with Mr. Paris,

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:55.960
in case we run
into any Kazon ships.

00:27:56.002 --> 00:27:57.401
Don't worry, Captain.

00:27:57.437 --> 00:27:58.904
You can count on me

00:27:58.939 --> 00:28:00.873
to keep those nefarious Kazon
at bay.

00:28:02.909 --> 00:28:04.001
Dismissed.

00:28:38.578 --> 00:28:40.876
What are you doing?

00:28:40.914 --> 00:28:43.542
I'm setting my tricorder
to emit a homing signal.

00:28:43.583 --> 00:28:44.948
What for?

00:28:45.051 --> 00:28:45.949
So when my people show up,

00:28:46.052 --> 00:28:47.314
they'll know
where to look for me.

00:28:47.354 --> 00:28:48.844
They won't come.

00:28:48.889 --> 00:28:50.049
They'll think you're dead.

00:28:50.090 --> 00:28:51.717
They're very persistent.

00:28:51.758 --> 00:28:53.521
I'm betting
they haven't given up on me.

00:28:53.560 --> 00:28:55.255
Well, maybe I should kill you

00:28:55.295 --> 00:28:56.819
and steal your technology

00:28:56.863 --> 00:28:58.831
and deliver it to my people.

00:28:58.865 --> 00:29:01.561
Then they'd have
to give me my name.

00:29:02.435 --> 00:29:04.062
You just won't give up,
will you?

00:29:07.307 --> 00:29:09.775
You won't stop me from earning
my name, Federation.

00:29:09.810 --> 00:29:12.779
Not Federation... Chakotay.

00:29:12.813 --> 00:29:14.906
That's my name.

00:29:14.981 --> 00:29:17.040
Did you have to earn it?

00:29:19.686 --> 00:29:21.916
No, not exactly.

00:29:22.022 --> 00:29:24.115
Then your name means nothing.

00:29:26.026 --> 00:29:28.494
My name was a gift...

00:29:28.528 --> 00:29:30.155
from my tribe.

00:29:30.197 --> 00:29:33.564
I cherish it
every day of my life.

00:29:35.468 --> 00:29:39.097
Just as I cherish
the Federation uniform.

00:29:39.139 --> 00:29:42.370
I should respect you
because you wear that uniform.

00:29:42.409 --> 00:29:45.344
Your name, my uniform...

00:29:45.378 --> 00:29:47.312
not much difference.

00:29:47.347 --> 00:29:48.609
We both have to earn them.

00:29:52.319 --> 00:29:54.879
What did you have to do
to earn your uniform?

00:29:54.921 --> 00:29:56.479
Study.

00:29:56.523 --> 00:30:00.289
Years of study.

00:30:00.327 --> 00:30:05.526
Learning about science
and ships and navigation.

00:30:05.565 --> 00:30:08.398
I suppose they don't expect you
to prove your battle skills.

00:30:08.435 --> 00:30:12.963
No. They prepared us
to defend ourselves in battle.

00:30:13.073 --> 00:30:15.541
They prepared us very well,

00:30:15.575 --> 00:30:17.941
and we had to pass
many difficult tests

00:30:17.978 --> 00:30:20.606
before we were given the right
to wear the uniform.

00:30:20.647 --> 00:30:22.478
You're saying that my name
and your uniform

00:30:22.515 --> 00:30:24.779
mean the same thing.

00:30:24.818 --> 00:30:25.910
But you're wrong.

00:30:25.952 --> 00:30:27.283
Why?

00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:29.515
What's so different about us?

00:30:29.556 --> 00:30:31.751
Aside from the fact that
I keep saving your life,

00:30:31.791 --> 00:30:33.588
and you keep
threatening to kill me?

00:30:33.627 --> 00:30:36.255
I must protect my territory.

00:30:36.296 --> 00:30:37.490
Territory is power.

00:30:37.530 --> 00:30:39.259
Let me tell you something.

00:30:39.299 --> 00:30:40.994
I have no interest
in your territory

00:30:41.067 --> 00:30:42.932
or anybody else's.

00:30:44.537 --> 00:30:46.801
My people taught me

00:30:46.840 --> 00:30:49.741
a man does not own land.

00:30:49.776 --> 00:30:52.609
He doesn't own anything

00:30:52.646 --> 00:30:55.308
but the courage and
loyalty in his heart.

00:30:55.348 --> 00:30:58.840
That's where my power
comes from.

00:31:00.587 --> 00:31:03.181
I think we both could use
some sleep, don't you?

00:33:12.118 --> 00:33:13.847
I've got a Kazon raider
approaching

00:33:13.887 --> 00:33:15.582
at bearing 288 mark 9.

00:33:15.622 --> 00:33:16.953
On screen.

00:33:18.324 --> 00:33:19.655
Open a channel.

00:33:21.861 --> 00:33:25.262
I'm Lieutenant Tom Paris
of the Starship Voyager.

00:33:25.298 --> 00:33:28.756
Jal Razik, first maje
of the Kazon-Ogla.

00:33:28.802 --> 00:33:30.633
I will speak to your Captain.

00:33:31.771 --> 00:33:34.501
I'm in command right now,
so you can speak to me.

00:33:37.377 --> 00:33:39.277
You are trespassing
in Ogla space.

00:33:39.312 --> 00:33:41.746
Why do you orbit our moon?

00:33:41.781 --> 00:33:44.272
Just stopped to make
a few repairs.

00:33:44.317 --> 00:33:45.909
We'll be on our way in no time.

00:33:45.952 --> 00:33:47.476
That is a lie.

00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:49.647
You are here looking
for your Commander Chakotay.

00:33:51.257 --> 00:33:53.748
Now, how would
you know about that?

00:33:53.793 --> 00:33:54.817
Quite simply.

00:33:54.861 --> 00:33:56.021
We killed him.

00:33:59.566 --> 00:34:01.295
Under what circumstances?

00:34:01.334 --> 00:34:02.926
He kidnapped a young man.

00:34:02.969 --> 00:34:04.129
During his escape,

00:34:04.170 --> 00:34:06.502
it became necessary
to destroy his ship.

00:34:06.539 --> 00:34:08.507
No doubt
you've found the remains.

00:34:08.541 --> 00:34:10.907
So I suggest you depart
immediately.

00:34:10.944 --> 00:34:13.071
Thanks for the advice.

00:34:13.113 --> 00:34:15.377
What a most unusual offer.

00:34:15.415 --> 00:34:17.906
A Kazon-Ogla maje

00:34:17.951 --> 00:34:21.785
allowing a trespasser
to leave his space unharmed.

00:34:21.821 --> 00:34:24.449
What would the other Kazon say

00:34:24.491 --> 00:34:27.619
about this new merciful attitude
of the Ogla?

00:34:27.660 --> 00:34:29.127
Don't tempt me, Talaxian.

00:34:29.162 --> 00:34:30.629
I would just as soon open fire.

00:34:30.663 --> 00:34:31.630
Would you?

00:34:31.664 --> 00:34:32.653
Neelix...

00:34:33.666 --> 00:34:36.533
No, I don't think so.

00:34:36.569 --> 00:34:40.630
That would attract
every rival Kazon sect

00:34:40.673 --> 00:34:43.198
to your secret training base,
wouldn't it?

00:34:43.243 --> 00:34:46.974
Now, I know your ships, Maje.

00:34:47.046 --> 00:34:50.982
I even sold a few Plaxan sensors
to the Ogla a few years back.

00:34:51.050 --> 00:34:53.177
I have no doubt

00:34:53.219 --> 00:34:54.880
that you read
the same life signs

00:34:54.921 --> 00:34:56.286
on that moon that we have.

00:34:56.322 --> 00:34:59.621
Perhaps one of those life signs
belongs to your Captain.

00:34:59.659 --> 00:35:01.593
If you've detected
the extensive weaponry

00:35:01.628 --> 00:35:03.357
deployed on the moon, know this.

00:35:03.396 --> 00:35:06.422
With one remote command,
I can cause that weaponry

00:35:06.466 --> 00:35:09.230
to self-destruct, destroying
the surface of the moon

00:35:09.269 --> 00:35:10.930
and everyone on it.

00:35:10.970 --> 00:35:13.706
Neither of us wants that, do we?

00:35:13.839 --> 00:35:16.330
Think of the cost of replacing
all those weapons.

00:35:16.375 --> 00:35:18.741
Awfully hard to come by
in this region.

00:35:18.777 --> 00:35:22.736
And it would make you
so vulnerable to your enemies.

00:35:22.781 --> 00:35:24.806
We'll leave as soon
as we've retrieved

00:35:24.850 --> 00:35:26.112
our crewmen... all of them,

00:35:26.151 --> 00:35:28.847
including Chakotay,
if he's alive.

00:35:28.887 --> 00:35:30.946
And if one of your people
is with him,

00:35:31.023 --> 00:35:32.490
he'll be returned to you.

00:35:34.793 --> 00:35:37.284
They're moving
into a lower orbit.

00:35:37.329 --> 00:35:39.126
Looks like they're intending
to enter the atmosphere.

00:35:39.164 --> 00:35:41.655
I need communication
with the surface, B'Elanna,

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:42.894
and soon.

00:35:42.935 --> 00:35:45.529
I still haven't been able to get
the dampening field working.

00:35:45.571 --> 00:35:48.540
I can't even give you
an estimate.

00:35:48.574 --> 00:35:50.064
Should we take Voyager down?

00:35:50.109 --> 00:35:51.974
I've already run
a soil analysis.

00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:53.840
The surface won't support
a landing.

00:35:53.879 --> 00:35:56.541
Then I guess the Captain's
going to be greeted

00:35:56.582 --> 00:35:58.413
by some unexpected visitors.

00:35:58.450 --> 00:36:00.577
At least
we bought her some time.

00:36:15.667 --> 00:36:17.225
Good morning.

00:36:17.269 --> 00:36:18.930
How did you sleep?

00:36:19.037 --> 00:36:20.334
Fine.

00:36:20.372 --> 00:36:21.896
Really?

00:36:21.940 --> 00:36:24.340
You seemed
a little restless to me.

00:36:24.376 --> 00:36:26.071
What do you mean?

00:36:26.111 --> 00:36:29.774
All that skulking around,
throwing things.

00:36:29.815 --> 00:36:31.180
You were awake?

00:36:31.216 --> 00:36:32.877
You think I'm going
to get much sleep

00:36:32.918 --> 00:36:35.352
around an Ogla warrior
who's threatened to kill me?

00:36:36.455 --> 00:36:38.787
Why didn't you
go through with it?

00:36:40.459 --> 00:36:41.448
I am a coward.

00:36:41.493 --> 00:36:43.051
I don't believe that.

00:36:43.095 --> 00:36:45.188
I don't believe you do, either.

00:36:45.230 --> 00:36:48.757
I think maybe you're beginning
to realize I'm not your enemy,

00:36:48.801 --> 00:36:51.531
and only a fool
would kill a friend.

00:36:51.570 --> 00:36:53.504
If you are my friend...

00:36:53.539 --> 00:36:55.769
then you're my only one.

00:36:59.044 --> 00:37:00.841
What happens to me now?

00:37:00.879 --> 00:37:02.176
Where do I go?

00:37:02.214 --> 00:37:04.808
Would any other Kazon sect
accept you?

00:37:04.850 --> 00:37:07.546
I would be a goven, an outcast.

00:37:07.586 --> 00:37:10.578
Each Kazon sect I meet
would cut one digit off,

00:37:10.622 --> 00:37:12.817
send me away.

00:37:12.858 --> 00:37:15.520
How many Kazon sects are there?

00:37:15.561 --> 00:37:16.926
It changes every day.

00:37:16.995 --> 00:37:18.860
Yesterday, there were 18.

00:37:18.897 --> 00:37:21.525
I guess you could come with us.

00:37:21.567 --> 00:37:23.831
To do what?
Dress in a uniform?

00:37:23.869 --> 00:37:25.496
You wouldn't have
to wear a uniform.

00:37:25.537 --> 00:37:27.368
And the closer you get
to your home,

00:37:27.406 --> 00:37:29.067
the farther I would be
from mine.

00:37:32.544 --> 00:37:34.512
If only you had killed me.

00:37:42.221 --> 00:37:44.485
Captain, four life-forms
approaching.

00:37:44.523 --> 00:37:45.922
40 meters.

00:37:45.958 --> 00:37:47.391
They appear to be Kazon.

00:37:52.264 --> 00:37:54.323
Please, put your weapons away.
We've come to help you.

00:37:54.366 --> 00:37:55.333
Help us?

00:37:55.367 --> 00:37:56.493
With what?

00:37:56.535 --> 00:37:58.560
We made contact with your ship

00:37:58.604 --> 00:38:00.663
and learned of the plight
of your missing crewman.

00:38:00.706 --> 00:38:03.607
We've come to offer
our assistance in finding him.

00:38:03.642 --> 00:38:05.735
That's very kind of you.

00:38:05.777 --> 00:38:07.904
You're walking
on very dangerous ground.

00:38:07.946 --> 00:38:10.278
There are concealed weapons
everywhere.

00:38:10.315 --> 00:38:12.783
Come.
We will lead you through them.

00:38:15.420 --> 00:38:16.751
Very well.

00:38:26.632 --> 00:38:28.930
Tell me
about the other uniforms...

00:38:29.001 --> 00:38:30.798
the ones the Kazon fought.

00:38:30.836 --> 00:38:32.861
The Trabe.

00:38:32.905 --> 00:38:34.702
The Kazon
shared their homeworld...

00:38:34.740 --> 00:38:37.072
if you can call it sharing.

00:38:37.109 --> 00:38:39.441
They had everything;
we had nothing.

00:38:39.478 --> 00:38:43.039
Until we took it from them
in the revolt 26 years ago.

00:38:44.416 --> 00:38:45.906
What is it?

00:38:45.951 --> 00:38:48.647
People coming this way.

00:38:48.687 --> 00:38:49.711
Humans and Kazon.

00:38:49.755 --> 00:38:52.053
What are we going to do?

00:38:52.090 --> 00:38:55.218
There's only one way back
to the Ogla for you

00:38:55.260 --> 00:38:56.852
and that's if you
earn your name.

00:38:58.530 --> 00:39:00.191
So I guess that's
what you'll have to do.

00:39:00.232 --> 00:39:02.393
But how?

00:39:03.502 --> 00:39:05.436
You're going to have to kill me.

00:39:12.744 --> 00:39:14.712
The signal seems to be coming
from some caves

00:39:14.746 --> 00:39:16.509
approximately 40 meters ahead.

00:39:16.548 --> 00:39:18.743
Your technology
continues to amaze us.

00:39:18.784 --> 00:39:20.911
It would have taken us
weeks to track them.

00:39:20.986 --> 00:39:23.784
After this is over, we have
to discuss an alliance.

00:39:23.822 --> 00:39:26.017
I would welcome
your friendship, Maje.

00:39:26.058 --> 00:39:27.923
Captain Janeway, I'm reading

00:39:27.960 --> 00:39:30.451
elevated... radiothermic
levels here.

00:39:30.495 --> 00:39:32.053
The Ocampa female is correct.

00:39:32.097 --> 00:39:34.122
This is a particularly
dangerous place.

00:39:34.166 --> 00:39:35.929
We lose many trainees here.

00:39:36.001 --> 00:39:38.367
Perhaps you would prefer
if we proceeded alone.

00:39:38.403 --> 00:39:39.768
They can't be far now.

00:39:39.805 --> 00:39:42.672
Thanks, but I think
we'll stick together.

00:39:42.708 --> 00:39:44.232
Voyager to away team.

00:39:44.276 --> 00:39:45.800
We're here, Mr. Paris.

00:39:45.844 --> 00:39:47.778
We finally broke through
the interference, Captain.

00:39:47.813 --> 00:39:48.802
Are you all right?

00:39:48.847 --> 00:39:49.814
We had a run-in...

00:39:49.848 --> 00:39:50.815
Everything is fine.

00:39:50.849 --> 00:39:52.646
We have the assistance
of the Ogla.

00:39:52.684 --> 00:39:56.245
That's what I was going
to tell you to expect.

00:39:56.288 --> 00:39:57.949
Can you lock on
to Commander Chakotay?

00:39:58.023 --> 00:39:59.047
Stand by.

00:40:00.592 --> 00:40:02.958
Voyager to Chakotay.
Do you read?

00:40:02.995 --> 00:40:04.622
I'm fine, Paris.

00:40:04.663 --> 00:40:06.961
Stand by for us
to beam you out of there.

00:40:07.032 --> 00:40:09.159
Belay that, Voyager.
Stand by.

00:40:09.201 --> 00:40:10.691
According to my readings,

00:40:10.736 --> 00:40:12.533
the away team's
only 50 meters away.

00:40:12.571 --> 00:40:13.799
Right, but don't...

00:40:13.839 --> 00:40:16.706
And alert Sick Bay to prepare
for a Code White resuscitation.

00:40:17.743 --> 00:40:19.301
Did you say "Code White"?

00:40:19.344 --> 00:40:20.436
Correct.

00:40:20.479 --> 00:40:21.912
I don't have time
to explain now.

00:40:21.947 --> 00:40:23.471
Chakotay out.

00:40:25.350 --> 00:40:26.408
It'll be all right.

00:40:26.451 --> 00:40:27.975
Our technology can revive me

00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:29.783
even if I'm brain-dead
for two minutes.

00:40:29.821 --> 00:40:31.345
Why are you doing this?

00:40:31.390 --> 00:40:32.448
Like you said,

00:40:32.491 --> 00:40:34.220
it's my fault
you don't have your name.

00:40:34.259 --> 00:40:36.352
I can't leave you
behind like this.

00:40:39.531 --> 00:40:41.795
Chakotay to away team.

00:40:41.833 --> 00:40:43.528
Good to hear your voice,
Commander.

00:40:43.568 --> 00:40:45.263
Captain, proceed with caution.

00:40:45.303 --> 00:40:48.272
I have been taken prisoner
by a young Kazon.

00:40:48.306 --> 00:40:49.637
He's threatening to kill me.

00:40:53.578 --> 00:40:54.602
This way.

00:40:54.646 --> 00:40:55.738
It's safer.

00:40:55.781 --> 00:40:57.112
I would beg to differ.

00:40:57.149 --> 00:40:59.481
Based on these readings,
that way

00:40:59.518 --> 00:41:01.713
would seem the logical choice.

00:41:01.753 --> 00:41:03.220
I must apologize for my comrade.

00:41:03.255 --> 00:41:05.689
I believe he's trying
to mislead you.

00:41:13.031 --> 00:41:16.091
So your technology
is not always an ally.

00:41:16.134 --> 00:41:18.659
Sometimes it betrays you... pity.

00:41:18.703 --> 00:41:20.534
I'm afraid
you would not score well

00:41:20.572 --> 00:41:23.006
in our training exercises.

00:41:29.915 --> 00:41:31.644
Away team to Voyager.

00:41:31.683 --> 00:41:34.584
Captain, that panel
is a micro-generator.

00:41:34.619 --> 00:41:35.586
You're right.

00:41:35.620 --> 00:41:36.917
If we can get a narrow beam

00:41:36.955 --> 00:41:38.889
through the field,
we can disable it.

00:41:38.924 --> 00:41:40.516
We could try remodulating
the phasers

00:41:40.559 --> 00:41:41.753
to a higher-frequency output.

00:41:41.793 --> 00:41:42.782
Make it fast.

00:41:50.669 --> 00:41:52.637
I've been waiting for you,
Razik.

00:41:54.840 --> 00:41:58.003
So, the Federation Commander
is your prisoner.

00:41:58.043 --> 00:41:59.408
I only came with him

00:41:59.444 --> 00:42:01.776
so I could have another
chance to kill him.

00:42:01.813 --> 00:42:04.111
So you could earn your name.

00:42:04.149 --> 00:42:06.276
That's what I've been
hoping for, Razik.

00:42:06.318 --> 00:42:08.616
But you taught me well.

00:42:08.653 --> 00:42:10.484
I know what you're going to say.

00:42:10.522 --> 00:42:12.581
You've said it
so many times before.

00:42:12.624 --> 00:42:15.991
In battle, there are
no second chances.

00:42:21.800 --> 00:42:23.768
But you are not my enemy.

00:42:23.802 --> 00:42:25.326
He is.

00:42:30.308 --> 00:42:33.072
My name is Jal Karden,
Kazon-Ogla.

00:42:38.083 --> 00:42:41.109
You are first maje now, Haliz.

00:42:41.153 --> 00:42:43.246
My life is yours.

00:42:50.028 --> 00:42:51.518
Kill me if you wish,

00:42:51.563 --> 00:42:54.589
or let me live and I will
follow you into battle

00:42:54.633 --> 00:42:56.396
whenever you command.

00:43:04.743 --> 00:43:06.574
Jal Karden.

00:43:09.581 --> 00:43:11.845
Kazon-Ogla.

00:43:11.883 --> 00:43:12.975
Kazon-Ogla.

00:43:17.389 --> 00:43:19.550
The Federation
does not belong here.

00:43:19.591 --> 00:43:23.083
If we meet again,
I will not hesitate to kill you.

00:43:24.362 --> 00:43:25.454
I understand.

00:43:33.338 --> 00:43:34.566
Janeway to Voyager.

00:43:34.606 --> 00:43:36.574
Five to beam up.

00:44:05.470 --> 00:44:07.700
A- koo-chee-moya.

00:44:07.739 --> 00:44:12.039
I pray on this day of memories

00:44:12.077 --> 00:44:14.602
to speak to my father...

00:44:14.646 --> 00:44:17.615
the one whom the wind
called Kolopak.

00:44:17.649 --> 00:44:21.312
Father, if you can hear me
among these unnamed stars,

00:44:21.353 --> 00:44:24.186
I ask you to continue
to watch over me

00:44:24.222 --> 00:44:25.917
as you've always done.

00:44:25.957 --> 00:44:31.122
I ask you also to watch over
a boy called Karden,

00:44:31.162 --> 00:44:34.131
who has a difficult path
to travel.

00:44:34.165 --> 00:44:36.895
A- koo-chee-moya.
